{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To find the range of the function \\( f(x, y, z) = xyz \\) subject to the constraints \\( x + y + z = 7 \\) and \\( x, y, z \\ge 0 \\), we need to analyze the behavior of \\( f \\) under these constraints.\n\n### Step 1: Identify the boundaries and critical points\n\nGiven the constraint \\( x + y + z = 7 \\), we can express \\( z \\) as \\( z = 7 - x - y \\). Substituting this into the function \\( f(x, y, z) \\), we get:\n\\[\nf(x, y, z) = xy(7 - x - y)\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Analyze the function at the boundaries\n\n1. **When one of the variables is zero:**\n   - If \\( x = 0 \\), then \\( f(0, y, z) = 0 \\cdot y \\cdot (7 - y - z) = 0 \\).\n   - If \\( y = 0 \\), then \\( f(x, 0, z) = x \\cdot 0 \\cdot (7 - x - z) = 0 \\).\n   - If \\( z = 0 \\), then \\( f(x, y, 0) = x \\cdot y \\cdot 7 = 7xy \\).\n\n2. **When two variables are zero:**\n   - If \\( x = 0 \\) and \\( y = 0 \\), then \\( z = 7 \\), and \\( f(0, 0, 7) = 0 \\).\n   - If \\( x = 0 \\) and \\( z = 0 \\), then \\( y = 7 \\), and \\( f(0, 7, 0) = 0 \\).\n   - If \\( y = 0 \\) and \\( z = 0 \\), then \\( x = 7 \\), and \\( f(7, 0, 0) = 0 \\).\n\n### Step 3: Find the maximum value\n\nTo find the maximum value, we need to consider the critical points where the partial derivatives of \\( f(x, y, z) \\) with respect to \\( x \\), \\( y \\), and \\( z \\) are zero.\n\n","prefix_end":1251,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,1477,279,2088,315,279,729,17767,282,2075,11,379,11,1147,8,284,40511,1124,8,3832,311,279,16982,17767,856,488,379,488,1147,284,220,22,1124,8,323,17767,856,11,379,11,1147,1124,709,220,15,1124,701,582,1184,311,23643,279,7709,315,17767,282,1124,8,1212,1493,16982,382,14374,14822,220,16,25,64547,279,22711,323,9023,3501,271,22043,279,21568,17767,856,488,379,488,1147,284,220,22,1124,701,582,646,3158,17767,1147,1124,8,438,17767,1147,284,220,22,